# Locks the exact text of the `range()` removal diagnostic (src/tychoc.c:3545).
# The message must name BOTH replacements and substitute the loop variable, so
# it can be copy-pasted: the three-clause `for` for a sequential count, and
# `parallel for i in 0..<N:` for a parallel one. Same discipline as
# tests/diag/dotlt_sequential.ty, which locks the mirror-image refusal.
#
# The reject lane cannot assert this: tests/run.sh:170-185 checks only that the
# exit is nonzero and stderr non-empty. This lane cmps stderr against
# tests/diag/range_removed.err (tests/run.sh:234-252).

fn main():
    for idx in range(0, 10, 2):
        println(str(idx))
